 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nget_module_part function always returns full dotted name instead of module part\n\n#### Description\n\nThe `get_module_part` function in `astroid.modutils` is not working correctly - it always returns the full dotted name instead of finding the actual importable module part.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom astroid import modutils\n\n# These should return the module part, not the full name\nprint(modutils.get_module_part('astroid.modutils.get_module_part'))\n# Expected: 'astroid.modutils'\n# Actual: 'astroid.modutils.get_module_part'\n\nprint(modutils.get_module_part('sys.path'))\n# Expected: 'sys' \n# Actual: 'sys.path'\n\nprint(modutils.get_module_part('math.log10'))\n# Expected: 'math'\n# Actual: 'math.log10'\n\n# This should raise ImportError for unknown modules\ntry:\n    modutils.get_module_part('unknown.module', modutils.__file__)\n    print(\"Should have raised ImportError!\")\nexcept ImportError:\n    print(\"Correctly raised ImportError\")\n```\n\nThe function seems to be bypassing the logic that should check if parts of the dotted name are actually importable modules and just returns the entire input string.\n</issue>\n",
